{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1360130-space-opera-realm-ideas-for-new-age-dreamspeaker","id":1360130,"title":"Space-Opera Realm Ideas For New Age Dreamspeaker","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-10T08:53:10-08:00","id":1360130,"title":"Space-Opera Realm Ideas For New Age Dreamspeaker","content":"Greetings all!<br /> <br /> I'm currently playing a New Age psychic in a crossover (WTA, V20, Demon, Changeling, etc). She is very into the entire New Age cosmology: angels, Ascended Masters (her totem is an Ascended Master) fairies, etc and that has brought her interests to space. Many New Age beliefs/religions exalt &quot;star-brothers&quot; or benevolent extraterrestrials that wish to hoist humanity into the Age of Aquarius.<br /> <br /> The plan is for her to travel to the Astral Umbra and visit a few space-opera themed realms (as opposed to more authentic, Deep Umbra space for now since she's only spirit 3) to gather allies among ET/science-fiction based Umbrood to help assist in her current campaign against the Wyrm on Earth. I'm looking for suggestions or ideas about how to integrate New Age themes with potential space operas and which kind of extraterrestrial astral spirits would be interested in working with a psychic. Also, what role(s) could she play within a particular science fiction-themed realm? What might be some quests that the respective umbrood send her on to prove her worthy of their assistance?<br /> <br /> Also, most interestingly: what sort of powers/weapons would these beings have that could distinguish them from traditional New Age entities? And how would you reflect any possible technology through M20's charms? (let's say a blaster or something of that sort)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","user":"KingJohn","date":". 01-10-2020, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T10:02:33-08:00","id":1360147,"title":"","content":"For quests to prove her worthiness to New Age aliens, remember that promoting Peace is a large undercurrent of belief. That these visitors from other worlds/dimensions are - aside from certain bad ones - generally enlightened, and actively work to promote peace and brotherhood throughout the galaxy. One of the reasons people claim these beings come here for is to help humanity overcome its atavistic urges, and mature as a species, so they can join the larger galactic/inter-dimensional community.<br /> <br /> Ergo, Umbrood patterned after this model might require that the mage work to bring a halt to hostilities between two groups and/or individuals on Earth, to prove she has the capacity to help mankind better itself. If she can act as intermediary, so two warring sides can stop fighting, reconcile as fellow humans, and work toward common goals, that might impress these Umbrood. The more people who are brought to peace, the longer they've been in conflict, and/or the more lasting the peace, the better. But it could be as simple as getting two people to drop a petty feud with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T12:02:05-08:00","id":1360180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1360130-space-opera-realm-ideas-for-new-age-dreamspeaker?p=1360147#post1360147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For quests to prove her worthiness to New Age aliens, remember that promoting Peace is a large undercurrent of belief. That these visitors from other worlds/dimensions are - aside from certain bad ones - generally enlightened, and actively work to promote peace and brotherhood throughout the galaxy. One of the reasons people claim these beings come here for is to help humanity overcome its atavistic urges, and mature as a species, so they can join the larger galactic/inter-dimensional community.<br /> <br /> Ergo, Umbrood patterned after this model might require that the mage work to bring a halt to hostilities between two groups and/or individuals on Earth, to prove she has the capacity to help mankind better itself. If she can act as intermediary, so two warring sides can stop fighting, reconcile as fellow humans, and work toward common goals, that might impress these Umbrood. The more people who are brought to peace, the longer they've been in conflict, and/or the more lasting the peace, the better. But it could be as simple as getting two people to drop a petty feud with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>What sorts of weapons/technology do you suspect they'd have to use if they needed to assist her on Earth?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T17:32:29-08:00","id":1360236,"title":"","content":"*Shrugs* Ray guns?<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, if we assume 1) the aliens desire peace and 2) they are hyper advanced, we can presume their weapons would go beyond mere killing tools (though they'd have those in abundance). They'd have weapons capable of pacifying without killing.<br /> <br /> Beams that stun. Sonic tones that manipulate the body, dropping blood pressure and making vision swim. Force fields. Combustion nullifiers. Dazzling lights, projected in a rainbow kaleidoscope, capable of hypnotizing the viewer. Launching large, thick globules of ectoplasm that stick to targets and arrest their movements. Heat rays that make weapons uncomfortable to hold. Releasing knock-out gas. Showing aggressors visions, overwhelming them with sensations and trying to encourage peace. Even straight up dropping people into pocket dimensions for a time, where they can do no harm.<br /> <br /> Imagine all the ways a fight could be concluded without killing the opponent, then imagine a race of beings sufficiently advanced enough to make those methods not only possible, but trivially easy to do without lethal force.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Now, how effective such abilities would be in practice is another matter. The ST will need to model such weapons as Umbrood Charms, leaving in the possibility they could fail. But that's par for the course, and simply having the option is worth the effort getting it. The real issue would be in the Umbrood crossing over and using them, without suffering too much to the Gauntlet or to Disbelief. But that's a tactical issue, that can be worked around. And hopefully, the Mage will be helping them cross over with Spirit 2.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-10-2020, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T17:51:30-08:00","id":1360242,"title":"","content":"As a follow-up, I imagine what it would look like for a New Age alien to appear in the material world would be as an idealized human (while New Age folk are not immune to envisioning their god-aliens as blond, blue-eyed white dudes, they could just as easily be androgynous and of ambiguous ethnicity; depends on how the ST wants to play it). They'd wear a silver jumpsuit, and have some kind of chrome utility belt around their waist. In a holster would be some sufficiently sci fi looking ray gun, except it has many more &quot;modes&quot; than simply lethal force. (See the above post for ideas).<br /> <br /> While all of these things would stand out anywhere except an SF convention, it wouldn't look impossible, which is the ideal form an Umbrood would want to take while visiting the material world. They might be chalked up as a cosplayer, or just a weirdo with a weird prop/gun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T11:13:34-08:00","id":1361305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1360130-space-opera-realm-ideas-for-new-age-dreamspeaker?p=1360236#post1360236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Shrugs* Ray guns?<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, if we assume 1) the aliens desire peace and 2) they are hyper advanced, we can presume their weapons would go beyond mere killing tools (though they'd have those in abundance). They'd have weapons capable of pacifying without killing.<br /> <br /> Beams that stun. Sonic tones that manipulate the body, dropping blood pressure and making vision swim. Force fields. Combustion nullifiers. Dazzling lights, projected in a rainbow kaleidoscope, capable of hypnotizing the viewer. Launching large, thick globules of ectoplasm that stick to targets and arrest their movements. Heat rays that make weapons uncomfortable to hold. Releasing knock-out gas. Showing aggressors visions, overwhelming them with sensations and trying to encourage peace. Even straight up dropping people into pocket dimensions for a time, where they can do no harm.<br /> <br /> Imagine all the ways a fight could be concluded without killing the opponent, then imagine a race of beings sufficiently advanced enough to make those methods not only possible, but trivially easy to do without lethal force.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Now, how effective such abilities would be in practice is another matter. The ST will need to model such weapons as Umbrood Charms, leaving in the possibility they could fail. But that's par for the course, and simply having the option is worth the effort getting it. The real issue would be in the Umbrood crossing over and using them, without suffering too much to the Gauntlet or to Disbelief. But that's a tactical issue, that can be worked around. And hopefully, the Mage will be helping them cross over with Spirit 2.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think their powers would require custom charms to be made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T11:23:16-08:00","id":1361306,"title":"","content":"I don't know/remember enough about Spirit Charms to make that judgement call. Some of them might be replicable with existing Charms. Some might require custom ones. It's up to the Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}